  "name": "persy",
  "description": "A high-performance transactional persistence engine written in Rust that implements ACID properties through a Copy-on-Write (CoW) architecture. It provides a single-file storage format with support for segmented record management, robust B-Tree indexing, and snapshot isolation. The system features a sophisticated page allocator, write-ahead logging (WAL) for crash recovery, and background operations for deferred flushing and maintenance.",
